\p
\v 1 In¦317066 the fifth¦317078 month¦317077 of the fourth¦317076 year¦317074 of the reign¦317069 of Yehudah's¦317073 King¦317071 Tsidkiyah¦317070 \add !(Zedekiah¦317070)\add*, Azzur's¦317084 son¦317082 Hananyah¦317081 who¦317086 was¦317087 a ‘prophet¦317085’ from¦317087 Gibeon¦317087, said¦317079 to¦317090 me¦317080 in¦317068 Yahweh's¦317089 \add ≈temple¦317088\add* as priests¦317091 and¦317092 all¦317092 the¦317094 people¦317094 \add watched\add*, saying¦317079,\x + \xo 28:1: \xt 2Ki 24:18-20; 2Ch 36:11-13.\x*
\v 2 “Yisrael's¦317103 god¦317102, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦317100 says¦317099: I've broken¦317105 the¦317108 yoke¦317108 of¦317102 the¦317109 Babylonian king¦317109.
\v 3 Within two¦317114 years¦317114, I¦317116, myself, will¦317117 bring¦317117 back¦317117 here all¦317124 the¦317126 utensils¦317126 from Yahweh's¦317128 residence that¦317129 the¦317133 Babylonian King¦317133 Nebuchadnezzar¦317131 got¦317130 from¦317136 this¦317139 place¦317120 and¦317140 took¦317130 to¦317118 Babylon¦317135.
\v 4 I¦317170, myself, will¦317161 \add ≈also¦317152\add* bring¦317161 Yekonyah (\add Jeconiah,\add* the son¦317146 of Yehudah's¦317151 King¦317149 Yehoyakim¦317148/\add Jehoiakim\add*) back¦317161 to¦317162 this¦317165 place¦317164, and¦317143 all¦317154 the¦317156 exiles¦317156 from Yehudah¦317157 that¦317165 were taken to Babylon¦317159, because¦317169 I'll¦317160 break¦317170 the¦317173 yoke¦317173 of¦317173 the¦317174 Babylonian king¦317174. That is Yahweh's¦317168 declaration¦317166.”
\p
\v 5 Then¦317177 the prophet Yirmeyah¦317178 spoke¦317177 to¦317180 the prophet Hananyah¦317182, as the priests¦317185 and¦317186 all¦317187 the¦317189 people¦317189 standing¦317190 in¦317191 Yahweh's¦317192 \add ≈temple¦317191\add* \add ≈watched\add*,
\v 6 saying¦317194, “Let it¦317194 be so¦317198—may¦317199 Yahweh do¦317199 all that. May¦317201 Yahweh \add ≈confirm\add* your¦317205 messages¦317205 that¦317206 you¦317207 prophesied¦317196, to bring¦317208 the¦317210 \add ≈temple¦317210 utensils¦317209\add* back¦317208 to¦317217 this¦317220 place¦317219, along with all the exiles¦317215 from¦317216 Babylon¦317216.
\v 7 However, please¦317226 listen to¦317224 this¦317228 message¦317227 that¦317229 I¦317230, myself, am¦317231 speaking¦317231 \add ≈as you and¦317233 all¦317234 the¦317236 people¦317236 listen\add*:
\v 8 The¦317245 prophets¦317238 who¦317239 \add ≈preceded\add* \add both\add* me and¦317242 you¦317242, prophesied¦317246 \add ≈long ago\add* that many¦317250 \add ≈nations¦317249\add* and¦317251 powerful¦317254 kingdoms¦317253 would experience wars¦317255, \add ≈terrible suffering\add*, and \add ≈deadly diseases\add*.
\v 9 The¦317264 prophet who¦317260 prophesies¦317261 about¦317262 peace¦317262, \add &that¦317260\add* prophet¦317265 will¦317266 be¦317266 known¦317266 as ‘a truthful¦317272 prophet sent¦317270 by Yahweh¦317271’ \add only\add* when¦317263 his message¦317264 comes¦317263 \add to pass\add*.”
\p
\v 10 Then¦317274 the prophet Hananyah¦317275 took¦317274 the yoke bar off the prophet Yirmeyah's¦317282 neck¦317281, and¦317274 broke¦317284 it¦317284.
\v 11 Then as all¦317289 the¦317291 people¦317291 watched, he¦317294 said¦317286, “This is what Yahweh¦317295 says¦317294: Just like that, I'll¦317297 break¦317297 the¦317300 yoke¦317300 of¦317300 the¦317303 Babylonian King¦317303 Nebuchadnezzar¦317302 off the neck¦317311 of¦317311 all¦317312 the¦317314 nations¦317314 within two¦317307 more years¦317307.”
