\v 20 Then Yirmeyah¦326241 \add ≈responded¦326240 to¦326242\add* all those who'd answered¦326258 him¦326259 including¦326240 both men¦326249 and¦326250 women¦326252. He¦326240 told¦326240 them all this message¦326260:
\v 21 Didn't Yahweh¦326281 remember¦326280 the incense¦326266 that¦326267 you all burned in¦326269 Yehudah's¦326270 cities¦326269 and on¦326283 Yerushalem's¦326272 streets¦326271—you and¦326274 your ancestors¦326274, your kings¦326275 and¦326276 leaders¦326276, and¦326277 the¦326277 people¦326277 of¦326277 the¦326278 land¦326278, and didn't¦326263 it¦326282 come¦326282 \add back\add* to his¦326285 \add ≈mind¦326285\add*?
\v 22 \add ≈Eventually¦326290,\add* he¦326289 could¦326289 no longer bear¦326292 it because of¦326293 your wicked¦326294 \add ≈behaviour\add*, \add i.e.,\add* because of the¦326297 detestable¦326297 \add <things\add* that¦326298 you all did¦326299. Then¦326287 your land¦326301 became¦326300 a \add ≈deserted¦326303 wasteland¦326303\add* and¦326287 a curse¦326304, without inhabitants¦326306 as¦326307 it is¦326289 today.
\v 23 \add ≈Because¦326319\add* you all \add ≈burnt¦326312 incense¦326312\add* \add to other gods\add* and¦326313 sinned¦326314 against Yahweh¦326315, and¦326316 because you wouldn't listen¦326317 to¦326318 his voice¦326318, his instructions¦326320, his¦326320 regulations¦326321, or his \add ≈promises\add*, this¦326331 disaster¦326330 has¦326328 \add ≈come¦326328 against\add* you as¦326332 \add you all can see\add* \add ≈today\add*.
\p
\v 24 Then Yirmeyah¦326337 told¦326336 all¦326340 the¦326342 people¦326342, \add ≈including¦326336\add* all¦326344 \add &those¦326346\add* women¦326346, “Listen¦326347 to¦326343 Yahweh's¦326350 message¦326348, all of¦326344 \add you from\add* Yehudah¦326353 who are \add now here\add* in¦326355 Egypt¦326356.
\v 25 Yisrael's¦326366 god¦326365, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦326362 says¦326361 that both you and¦326369 your wives¦326369 have¦326370 said¦326370 \add ≈out loud¦326386\add* and \add ≈confirmed with¦326372 your actions\add* that you'll all certainly¦326376 carry¦326389 out your vows¦326380 to worship the¦326384 queen¦326384 of¦326384 the¦326385 skies¦326385 and¦326386 to¦326386 pour¦326386 out¦326386 drink¦326388 offerings¦326388 to her¦326387. \add ≈So then, go ahead and do those things to fulfill¦326373 your wows\add*.
\v 26 So¦326401 then all¦326406 of¦326406 Yehudah who're staying¦326409 Egypt, listen to Yahweh's¦326405 message¦326403: Yahweh says¦326416, listen, I've promised by¦326414 my¦326414 \add ≈powerful¦326415\add* name that¦326409 none of the¦326415 men¦326429 from Yehudah who're living¦326409 \add here\add* in¦326410 Egypt will¦326420 call on my¦326422 name¦326423 any¦326427 more, i.e., you'll all \add ≈no longer\add* say¦326431, ‘As \add #our\add* master¦326434 Yahweh lives¦326409.’
\v 27 Listen, I'm¦326441 watching¦326442 over¦326443 them¦326443 for¦326444 disaster¦326444 and¦326445 not¦326445 for¦326446 good¦326446. Every¦326448 Judean person¦326450 in¦326453 Egypt¦326455 will¦326447 \add ≈meet¦326447 their¦326447 end¦326460 through¦326456 war or\add* famine¦326457 until¦326458 they're all eliminated.
\v 28 Then¦326462 \add a few\add* survivors¦326462 \add from the battles\add* will¦326464 return¦326464 from¦326465 Egypt¦326468 to Yehudah¦326470 \add ≈region¦326467\add*—only a small number¦326472 of¦326467 them¦326489. \add ≈In that¦326478 way,\add* all¦326474 the \add ≈remaining Judens\add* who¦326478 went¦326478 to live¦326482 in Egypt will know¦326473 whose word¦326484 will¦326487 stand—\add ≈mine or theirs\add*.
\v 29 Yahweh¦326497 declares¦326495 that this will be¦326494 the¦326494 sign¦326494 for you all: I'm going to¦326500 punish you all in¦326503 this place¦326503 so¦326505 that¦326505 you'll know¦326506 that¦326507 \add ≈what I've said will¦326509 come to pass, resulting in\add* harm¦326512 for all of¦326495 you.
\v 30 Yahweh¦326518 says¦326517: Listen, I'm¦326519 about¦326520 to¦326520 \add ≈hand¦326528\add* the Egyptian¦326527 king, Far-oh¦326523 \add !(Pharaoh¦326523)\add* Hofra¦326524 over to his¦326529 enemies¦326529 and¦326530 to those¦326531 who¦326531 want¦326531 to kill him. It'll be¦326520 the same as¦326533 when I¦326534 \add ≈handed¦326534\add* Yehudah's¦326540 King Tsidkiyah¦326537 \add !(Zedekiah¦326537)\add* king¦326538 of¦326538 Judah¦326540 over to the¦326541 Babylonian King Nebuchadnezzar¦326542—his enemy¦326546 who¦326547 \add ≈wanted¦326547 him dead\add*.\x + \xo 44:30: \xt 2Ki 25:1-7.\x*
